---
// Figures: one slow command (mode="keys") and freeing a big key (mode="free").
// The same model and drawing: the main thread at millisecond scale, a client
// that sends PING about once a millisecond, and one expensive job.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Slider from '../shared/Slider.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './redis.css';
interface Props { number: number; mode: 'keys' | 'free' }
const { number, mode } = Astro.props;
const id = mode === 'keys' ? 'redis-slow-command' : 'redis-free';
const title = mode === 'keys' ? 'One slow command stops everyone' : 'Freeing a big key: DEL, UNLINK and expiry';
const caption = mode === 'keys'
  ? 'Model, slowed 50 times, with costs I measured on a laptop: KEYS * took 99.4 ms of main-thread time for 1,000,000 keys and scales with the number of keys; an ordinary request takes about 7 µs. 400 other requests a second arrive at random; one client sends PING, waits for the reply, sleeps 1 ms and repeats, as my probe did. The chart draws each PING as a stem at the moment it was sent, on a fixed scale up to one second, and keeps the last two seconds so you can compare runs. Left out: the time to send KEYS’s large reply, which the client also waits for, and I/O threads.'
  : 'Model, slowed 50 times, with costs I measured on a laptop: freeing a set of 2,000,000 members took 195 ms. UNLINK hands the same work to a background thread. The expiry cases use lazyfree-lazy-expire no (the default in Redis 8.10.3) and yes; the key is found by the expiry cycle, which runs 10 times a second by default. A command that touches the key after its TTL has run out would free it in the same way. 400 other requests a second; one client sends PING about once a millisecond, drawn as a stem at the moment it was sent. Left out: the few milliseconds of delay I measured with every background free (see the text), and allocator contention between the two threads.';
---
<SimFigure number={number} id={id} title={title} advance={2000} clock={false}
  legend={mode === 'keys'
    ? [{ kind: 'redis', label: 'KEYS running' }, { kind: 'neutral', label: 'Other requests' }, { kind: 'client', label: 'PING waiting, and its round trip' }]
    : [{ kind: 'redis', label: 'Freeing memory' }, { kind: 'neutral', label: 'Other requests' }, { kind: 'client', label: 'PING waiting, and its round trip' }]}
  caption={caption}>
  <Fragment slot="params">
    {mode === 'keys'
      ? <Slider name="keys" label="Keys in the database" min={0} max={4} value={2} />
      : <Choice name="job" label="How the key goes" value="del"
          options={[{ value: 'del', label: 'DEL' }, { value: 'unlink', label: 'UNLINK' }, { value: 'expire', label: 'TTL runs out' }, { value: 'expire-lazy', label: 'TTL runs out, lazy-expire yes' }]} />}
    <button type="button" class="cache-button cache-primary redis-action" data-run>{mode === 'keys' ? 'Run KEYS *' : 'Run DEL bigset'}</button>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="ran" label={mode === 'keys' ? 'KEYS blocked the thread for' : 'Main thread blocked for'} kind="redis" />
    <Readout name="worst" label="Slowest PING this run" kind="client" />
    <Readout name="queue" label="Requests waiting now" kind="client" />
    <Readout name="time" label="Redis time" />
  </Fragment>
  <div data-strip data-mode={mode}></div>
  <div slot="after" data-chart></div>
  <p slot="after" class="redis-status" data-status aria-live="polite"></p>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    {mode === 'keys' ? <>
      <p>A timeline of Redis's main thread over the last 400 ms, with a lane below it for the probing client's PING. Normally the thread shows only thin slivers of work: about 400 small requests a second and a PING about once a millisecond, each taking a few microseconds. The chart below has one stem per PING, as tall as its round trip, on a fixed scale from 0 to 1,000 ms; normally every stem is about 0.1 ms, too short to see.</p>
      <p>Pressing Run KEYS * puts one long block on the timeline. With a million keys it lasts about 100 ms. While it runs, the PING that arrived waits for all of it, drawn as a bar in the PING lane, and about 40 other requests pile up behind it; the chart shows a single stem of about 100 ms. Then the queue drains in well under a millisecond and round trips return to 0.1 ms. With 10 million keys the block lasts about a second and the stem is ten times taller, reaching the top of the chart beside the earlier one; with 100,000 keys it is about 10 ms.</p>
    </> : <>
      <p>Two timelines over the last 400 ms: Redis's main thread, and a background thread that Redis uses for freeing memory, with a lane below for the probing client's PING. The chart below has one stem per PING, as tall as its round trip, on a fixed scale from 0 to 250 ms.</p>
      <p>With DEL, freeing the 2,000,000-member set takes 195 ms on the main thread, and the PING waiting behind it takes about 195 ms. With UNLINK, the main thread only unlinks the key (a few microseconds) and the background thread spends the same 195 ms freeing the memory; PING round trips stay near 0.1 ms. When the key's TTL runs out instead, the server frees it on the main thread at the next expiry cycle, exactly like DEL, because lazy freeing on expiry is off by default in Redis. With lazyfree-lazy-expire yes, the expired key is freed on the background thread, as with UNLINK.</p>
    </>}
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { mountSim, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { stemChart } from './stems.mjs';
  import { mainThread, jobFor, NET, REQUEST } from './mainthread-model.mjs';
  import { threadStrip, scaled } from './strip.mjs';

  const PER_MS = 20; // µs of Redis time for each millisecond on screen: slowed 50 times
  const WINDOW = 400000; // µs shown in the timeline
  const KEY_STOPS = [100000, 300000, 1000000, 3000000, 10000000];
  const keysText = (n: number) => (n >= 1e6 ? `${n / 1e6} million` : `${(n / 1000).toLocaleString('en-GB')},000`);
  const ms = (us: number) => (us >= 10000 ? `${Math.round(us / 1000)} ms` : us >= 1000 ? `${(us / 1000).toFixed(1)} ms` : `${(us / 1000).toFixed(2)} ms`);

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="redis-slow-command"], [data-figure-id="redis-free"]').forEach(root => {
    const mode = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-strip]')!.dataset.mode;
    const keysMode = mode === 'keys';
    const run = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-run]')!;
    const status = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-status]')!;
    const step = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-advance]');
    if (step) {
      step.querySelector('span')!.textContent = 'Step 40 ms';
      step.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Step forward 40 milliseconds of Redis time');
    }
    const strip = threadStrip(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-strip]')!, {
      label: keysMode ? 'Timeline of the Redis main thread, and of a PING waiting for it' : 'Timelines of the Redis main thread and the background lazy-free thread, and of a PING waiting',
      lanes: keysMode
        ? [{ id: 'main', label: 'Main thread', short: 'Main' }, { id: 'ping', label: 'PING', short: 'PING' }]
        : [{ id: 'main', label: 'Main thread', short: 'Main' }, { id: 'bg', label: 'Lazy-free thread', short: 'Free' }, { id: 'ping', label: 'PING', short: 'PING' }],
      laneHeight: 34,
      format: (v: number) => `${Math.round(v / 1000)} ms`,
      axisLabel: 'Redis time (ms)',
    });
    // A fixed scale, so a stall ten times longer draws a stem ten times taller, and a
    // two-second window, so the previous run's stem is still there to compare.
    const chart = stemChart(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-chart]')!, {
      label: 'Round trip of each PING, in milliseconds, drawn at the moment it was sent, over Redis time',
      height: 200,
      kind: 'client',
      x: { label: 'Redis time (ms)', window: keysMode ? 2000 : 1000, format: (v: number) => `${Math.round(v)}` },
      y: { label: 'PING round trip (ms)', domain: [0, keysMode ? 1000 : 250], format: (v: number) => `${Math.round(v)}` },
    });

    const params = () => {
      const job = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-param="job"]:checked')?.value ?? 'del';
      const index = Number(root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-param="keys"]')?.value ?? 2);
      return { job, keys: KEY_STOPS[index] };
    };
    const showKeys = () => {
      const output = root.querySelector('[data-param-output="keys"]');
      if (output) output.textContent = keysText(params().keys);
      root.querySelector('[data-param="keys"]')?.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', `${keysText(params().keys)} keys`);
    };
    const runLabel = () => {
      if (keysMode) return 'Run KEYS *';
      return { del: 'Run DEL bigset', unlink: 'Run UNLINK bigset', expire: 'Let bigset expire', 'expire-lazy': 'Let bigset expire' }[params().job as 'del'];
    };
    let shown: any = null, drawn = 0, since = 0;

    const sim = mountSim(root, {
      seed: 4,
      create: () => scaled(mainThread({}, 4), PER_MS),
      update: () => { showKeys(); run.textContent = runLabel(); return true; },
      render(model: any) {
        const m = model.inner;
        if (m !== shown) { shown = m; drawn = 0; chart.clear(); }
        const now = m.sim.now;
        m.trim(WINDOW + 50000);
        for (; drawn < m.pings.length; drawn++) chart.push(m.pings[drawn].sent / 1000, m.pings[drawn].rtt / 1000);
        chart.render();
        const from = Math.max(0, now - WINDOW);
        const blocks = m.blocks.filter((b: any) => b.end >= from && b.start <= now).map((b: any) => ({
          lane: b.lane, start: b.start, end: Math.min(b.end, now),
          kind: b.kind === 'job' || b.kind === 'free' ? 'redis' : 'socket',
          label: b.kind === 'job' ? (keysMode ? 'KEYS *' : b.label.startsWith('key expires') ? 'expire bigset' : b.label === 'DEL' ? 'DEL bigset' : 'UNLINK') : b.kind === 'free' ? 'freeing bigset' : undefined,
        }));
        // The PING in flight, if it is waiting at the server, and recent PINGs that waited.
        const waits: any[] = [];
        for (const p of m.pings) {
          const arrived = p.sent + NET, served = p.t - NET - REQUEST;
          if (served - arrived > 300 && p.t >= from) waits.push({ lane: 'ping', start: arrived, end: served, kind: 'client', label: 'PING waiting' });
        }
        const job = m.lastJob;
        if (job && m.pending && job.requested <= now) {
          // A PING sent before the job finishes waits at the server until it does.
          const last = m.pings.at(-1);
          const sentAfter = last ? last.t + 1000 : 0;
          const arrived = sentAfter + NET;
          if (now - arrived > 300) waits.push({ lane: 'ping', start: arrived, end: now, kind: 'client', label: 'PING waiting' });
        }
        strip.render({ from, to: Math.max(WINDOW, now), blocks: blocks.concat(waits), now });

        const worst = m.pings.filter((p: any) => p.t >= since).reduce((w: number, p: any) => Math.max(w, p.rtt), 0);
        setReadouts(root, {
          ran: job ? (job.finished != null ? (job.main < 1000 ? `${Math.round(job.main)} µs` : ms(job.main)) : m.pending ? 'running…' : '–') : '–',
          worst: worst ? ms(worst) : '–',
          queue: String(m.waiting()),
          time: `${(now / 1e6).toFixed(2)} s`,
        });
        run.disabled = m.pending > 0;
        if (job && job.finished != null && !m.pending && !status.dataset.done) {
          status.dataset.done = '1';
          status.textContent = keysMode
            ? `KEYS * finished after ${ms(job.main)}; every request that arrived meanwhile waited for it.`
            : job.label === 'UNLINK' ? `UNLINK bigset returned after ${Math.round(job.main)} µs; the background thread spent ${ms(job.bg)} freeing the memory.`
            : job.label === 'DEL' ? `DEL bigset finished: the main thread was blocked for ${ms(job.main)}.`
            : job.bg ? `bigset expired at the next expiry cycle; with lazyfree-lazy-expire yes the background thread spent ${ms(job.bg)} freeing it.`
            : `bigset expired at the next expiry cycle and was freed on the main thread, which was blocked for ${ms(job.main)}.`;
        }
      },
    });
    run.textContent = runLabel();
    showKeys();
    run.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const p = params();
      const m = sim.model.inner;
      since = m.sim.now;
      delete status.dataset.done;
      m.run(jobFor(keysMode ? 'keys' : p.job, { keys: p.keys }));
      status.textContent = keysMode
        ? `KEYS * sent over ${keysText(p.keys)} keys.`
        : p.job.startsWith('expire') ? 'bigset’s TTL has run out; the next expiry cycle will find it.' : `${p.job.toUpperCase()} bigset sent.`;
      if (!sim.playing) sim.play();
    });
    root.querySelector('[data-reset]')?.addEventListener('click', () => { status.textContent = ''; delete status.dataset.done; since = 0; });
  });
</script>
